**🟢 Best Practice: Potential Memory Leak - Opener Reference**

**File:** `app/javascript/controllers/popup_form_controller.js` **Line:** 6

The code nulls window.opener before reloading but doesn't handle cleanup if reload fails or if the popup is closed without successful submission.

**Current Code:**
```javascript
handleSubmitEnd(event) {
  if (event.detail.success) {
    if (window.opener && !window.opener.closed) {
      const opener = window.opener
      window.opener = null
      // ...
    }
    window.close()
  }
}
```

**Suggested Fix:**
```javascript
disconnect() {
  // Clean up opener reference when controller disconnects
  if (window.opener) {
    window.opener = null
  }
}

handleSubmitEnd(event) {
  // ... existing code
}
```

**Recommendation:** Add a disconnect() lifecycle hook to properly clean up the opener reference when the controller is destroyed.

---
